                    <tr>
                      <td background="images/gray.gif"><!-- NP v3.7.4 -->
                        <a name="newsitem961471466,10900,"></a>
                        <p>
                      
	<!-- NP v3.7.4 -->
	<a name="newsitem983261939,66286,"></a>
<table  width="100%" border=2 bordercolor="black" bordercolordark="#333333" bordercolorlight="#666666" cellpadding=3 background="gray.gif"><tr>	<td><FONT face="Arial" size="2"><BR><B><U>Looking for Site Admin</U></B><br> <small>-<b>Xian</b> : Tuesday, February 27, 2001</small><br><br><FONT face="Arial" size="2">Due to other projects Lux and myself can no longer keep up with running www.seventhhammernews.net and are looking for someone to run this site! Please drop Lux and email at sbenson@gamerealm.com if you are interested, we are also looking for people to help update the news.<br></FONT> <font size="-1"><center><a href="#top">-Top-</a></font></center></td></tr></table><br>
<a name="newsitem981582176,3784,"></a>
<table  width="100%" border=2 bordercolor="black" bordercolordark="#333333" bordercolorlight="#666666" cellpadding=3 background="gray.gif"><tr>	<td><FONT face="Arial" size="2"><BR><B><U>Scheduled Downtime - 02/07/01</U></B><br> <small>-<b>Xian</b> : Wednesday, February 7, 2001</small><br><br><FONT face="Arial" size="2">Source: Whineplay<br><br>You should check the scheduled downtime section of our web site for further details (it should be updated shortly). But we will be taking one server down each day starting Wednesday so that we can do some hardware upgrades on them. We will be starting on with E'ci on Wednesday (7th), Innoruuk on Thursday (8th), and Fennin Ro on Friday (9th). They will be coming down at about 8 am PST, and will be down for about 8 hours. We'll be doing the same for all the servers, and we'll let you know the schedule for them as soon as we can. <br>Three other servers will be coming down for scheduled maintenance on Wednesday (unrelated to the upgrades). Brell, Rathe and Lanys will be coming down for about 6 hours, starting at about 3 am PST. <br><br>We're sorry for the inconvenience, but this sort of maintenance is necessary to maintain these servers and to keep the game running smoothly. <br><br>- Alan<br></FONT> <font size="-1"><center><a href="#top">-Top-</a></font></center></td></tr></table><br>
<a name="newsitem981580200,37014,"></a>
<table  width="100%" border=2 bordercolor="black" bordercolordark="#333333" bordercolorlight="#666666" cellpadding=3 background="gray.gif"><tr>	<td><FONT face="Arial" size="2"><BR><B><U>Safe Auctions?</U></B><br> <small>-<b>Lux</b> : Wednesday, February 7, 2001</small><br><br><FONT face="Arial" size="2">With all the recent rumors of players losing their accounts due to auctions I wanted to take a minute to remind players we are running our own auction site at <a href="http://www.playerauctions.com">www.playerauctions.com</a>.<br></FONT> <font size="-1"><center><a href="#top">-Top-</a></font></center></td></tr></table><br>
<a name="newsitem981516364,86022,"></a>
<table  width="100%" border=2 bordercolor="black" bordercolordark="#333333" bordercolorlight="#666666" cellpadding=3 background="gray.gif"><tr>	<td><FONT face="Arial" size="2"><BR><B><U>Kurns Tower Raid</U></B><br> <small>-<b>Xian</b> : Tuesday, February 6, 2001</small><br><br><FONT face="Arial" size="2">The guild Revenantes will be holding a raid on The Seventh Hammer sever in Kurns Tower at 7pm PST on Saturday, February 10th. All levels 10 through 24 are welcome to attend. <br><br>For more information send a tell to Sabram on Seventh Hammer. The goal of the raid is for at least 5 people to gain levels or 1 monk to get all the fingers for the Shackle of rock.<br></FONT> <font size="-1"><center><a href="#top">-Top-</a></font></center></td></tr></table><br>
<a name="newsitem981515482,27587,"></a>
<table  width="100%" border=2 bordercolor="black" bordercolordark="#333333" bordercolorlight="#666666" cellpadding=3 background="gray.gif"><tr>	<td><FONT face="Arial" size="2"><BR><B><U>Site loading time</U></B><br> <small>-<b>Lux</b> : Tuesday, February 6, 2001</small><br><br><FONT face="Arial" size="2">The site loading time has been slow lately due to the connection tool we use to see who's online. The host of the tool seems to be down a lot and every time they are down it is slowing our site to a crawl. I will be removing the connection tool until they prove to be more stable.<br></FONT> <font size="-1"><center><a href="#top">-Top-</a></font></center></td></tr></table><br>
<a name="newsitem981512572,17016,"></a>
<table  width="100%" border=2 bordercolor="black" bordercolordark="#333333" bordercolorlight="#666666" cellpadding=3 background="gray.gif"><tr>	<td><FONT face="Arial" size="2"><BR><B><U>Speed cheat</U></B><br> <small>-<b>Xian</b> : Tuesday, February 6, 2001</small><br><br><FONT face="Arial" size="2">Rumors are flying around there is a speed hack/cheat floating around and is usable with Everquest. I don't want to post the URL of the sites talking about it so I will post some of the comments from players using the cheat.<br><br>"Its fun running across the zone instantly"<br><br>"O yea and backstab recharges instantly so do your other skills and you can "super camp" so you camp in id say...... 3 seconds or less"<br><br>"Well I've been using this for a few days now, things I've learned:<br>1) It is capable of SoWing you at will<br>2) Stay away from water, as it speeds up oxygen consumption, and you will die in under a second (@ 32x)<br>3) It is seemingly undectable...have used it w/ gm's in the zone. I would guess that the only way you're gonna get caught is if you set your speed to high and someone reports you or a GM sees you flying across the zone,,,(invis yourself if possible)<br>4) Dosnt do squat for backstab, bind wounds, etc...buttons pop up again, but when pressed, they say you need more time before doing it again (does this raise a flag?)<br>5) APPEARS to make your buffs wear off quicker, but as soon as you zone, they show up again<br>6) Appears to compress time, visually at least"<br><br>"If you do decide to use the speedhack I highly recommend you do not go above sow speed. I'm sure that the servers have checks that say "If the player goes more than X units in Y seconds, he is cheating" which would raise a flag and they would investigate it further. Saying "Well I went up to warp 9 with GMs in the zone and I didn't get banned!" means nothing since Verant doesn't even ban people on the spot. They usually wait for a while to investigate or do further checks or something. It will not affect your weapon speeds because that is stored serverside (and trying to increase weapon speeds probably raises a flag). Basically if you like your characters and your account don't do anything that's not possible within the normal game."<br><br><a href="http://forums.gamerealm.com/cgi-bin/showflat.pl?Cat=75,76,77,45,46&Board=newscomments7th&Number=26860&page=0&view=collapsed&sb=5&part=&vc=">Comments</a>?<br></FONT> <font size="-1"><center><a href="#top">-Top-</a></font></center></td></tr></table><br>
<a name="newsitem981444659,24130,"></a>
<table  width="100%" border=2 bordercolor="black" bordercolordark="#333333" bordercolorlight="#666666" cellpadding=3 background="gray.gif"><tr>	<td><FONT face="Arial" size="2"><BR><B><U>Test Server Patch Message </U></B><br> <small>-<b>Xian</b> : Monday, February 5, 2001</small><br><br><FONT face="Arial" size="2">These are the latest patch message from off of the Test Server:<br><br>February 2nd, 7:00pm<br>-------------------------<br>1) Superior Healing moved to level 51 for shamans and druids. casting difficulty reduced<br>2) New level 55 Druid and shaman spell, Chloroblast, similar to remedy for clerics. <br>3) New Druid spell at level 60, upgrade to superior healing, Natures Touch.<br>4) Paladins:<br>a) Add Endure Magic spell at level 30<br>b) Add Resist Magic at 55<br>c) Move Guard spell from 49 to 39<br>d) Move Armor of Faith from 53 to 49<br>e) New level 53 paladin spell, Divine Glory, clone of divine strength but 100 hp instead of 200<br>f) New level 59 spell, Celestial Cleansing 110 hp healdot per tick, for 4 ticks. 1.5 second casting time. Recast time 30 secs.<br>g) Defense skill cap made exactly same as warriors<br>5) Shadowknights:<br>a) Remove artificially inflated mana cost for pre level 50 lifetap spells<br>b) Move Spirit Tap to level 55<br>c) Move Drain Spirit to level 57<br>d) Add Drain Soul at level 60<br>e) Grim Aura added at level 22<br>f) Move Shieldskin to level 34<br>g) Mini Intensify Death pet buff added at 29, 10% (min) haste 5 str 5 ac<br>h) Add Diamondskin spell at 59<br>i) Defense skill cap made exactly same as warriors<br>6) Rangers:<br>a) Add Endure Cold at 22<br>b) Add Skin Like Nature at 59<br>c) Add FireFist at 22<br>d) Move Bramblecoat from 49 to 39<br>e) Add Spikecoat at 49<br>f) Add resist cold at 55<br>g) Add Panic Animal at 22<br>i) Offense and weapons skill made identical to warriors<br>7) Bards:<br>a) Cassindra`s Chant of Clarity for Bards at level 20<br>b) Bards defensive skill made exactly the same as a warriors<br><br>8) Magicians<br>a) New level 59 spell, Valiant Companion, makes pet immune to fear (own pet only)<br>b) New level 39 spell, Summon Companion, if pet not noticed by any hostile npcs, pet returns to you instantly.<br>c) Rain spells no longer count pets against total number of entities they can damage (all rain spells)<br>d) Expedience for Mages at level 29. Target casters pet, J Boot speed buff for pet only<br><br>9) Warriors<br>a) Aggressive and Defensive disciplines fixed before they would only affect damage taken and not affect damage dealt out. Now they affect both as designed.<br><br>10) New Scrolls are temporarily avaiable in East Commons<br><br><a href="http://forums.gamerealm.com/cgi-bin/showflat.pl?Cat=75,76,77,45,46&Board=newscomments7th&Number=26106&page=0&view=collapsed&sb=5">Comments</a>?<br></FONT> <font size="-1"><center><a href="#top">-Top-</a></font></center></td></tr></table><br>
<a name="newsitem981358230,65920,"></a>
<table  width="100%" border=2 bordercolor="black" bordercolordark="#333333" bordercolorlight="#666666" cellpadding=3 background="gray.gif"><tr>	<td><FONT face="Arial" size="2"><BR><B><U>Test Server Rumors</U></B><br> <small>-<b>Xian</b> : Sunday, February 4, 2001</small><br><br><FONT face="Arial" size="2">Source</a href="http://www.planeteverquest.com/cazicthule">Planet Everquest</a><br><br>Players on the test server are reporting some interesting changes. As always, just because something appears on the test server does not mean they are going to be taken to the live servers. But here's a hint as to what might come, posted by Scary_Grant on the Sony Boards:<br><br>1) Superior Healing moved to level 51 for shamans and druids. casting difficulty reduced<br><br>2) New level 55 Druid and shaman spell, Chloroblast, similar to remedy for clerics.<br><br>3) New Druid spell at level 60, upgrade to superior healing, Natures Touch.<br><br>4) Paladins:<br>Add Endure Magic spell at level 30 <br>Add Resist Magic at 55 <br>Move Guard spell from 49 to 39 <br>Move Armor of Faith from 53 to 49 <br>New level 53 paladin spell, Divine Glory, clone of divine strength but 100 hp instead of 200 <br>New level 59 spell, Celestial Cleansing 110 hp healdot per tick, for <br><br>4 ticks. 1.5 second casting time. Recast time 30 secs. <br>Defense skill cap made exactly same as warriors<br><br>5) Shadowknights:<br>Remove artificially inflated mana cost for pre level 50 lifetap spells <br>Move Spirit Tap to level 55 <br>Move Drain Spirit to level 57 <br>Add Drain Soul at level 60 <br>Grim Aura added at level 22 <br>Move Shieldskin to level 34 <br>Mini Intensify Death pet buff added at 29, 10% (min) haste 5 str 5 ac <br>Add Diamondskin spell at 59 <br>Defense skill cap made exactly same as warriors<br><br>6) Rangers:<br>Add Endure Cold at 22 <br>Add Skin Like Nature at 59 <br>Add FireFist at 22 <br>Move Bramblecoat from 49 to 39 <br>Add Spikecoat at 49 <br>Add resist cold at 55 <br>Add Panic Animal at 22 <br>Offense and weapons skill made identical to warriors<br><br>7) Bards:<br>Cassindra`s Chant of Clarity for Bards at level 20. Bards defensive skill made exactly the same as a warriors<br><br>8) Magicians<br>New level 59 spell, Valiant Companion, makes pet immune to fear (own pet only). New level 39 spell, Summon Companion, if pet not noticed by any hostile npcs, pet returns to you instantly. <br>Rain spells no longer count pets against total number of entities they can damage (all rain spells). Expedience for Mages at level 29. Target casters pet, J Boot speed buff for pet only<br><br>9) Warriors<br>Aggressive and Defensive disciplines fixed before they would only affect damage taken and not affect damage dealt out. Now they affect both as designed.<br><br>10) New Scrolls are temporarily available in East Commons<br>This is on the TEST SERVER only. There is no guarantee any of these changes will actually go live.<br><br><a href="http://forums.gamerealm.com/cgi-bin/showflat.pl?Cat=75,76,77,45,46&Board=generalseventh&Number=26106&page=0&view=collapsed&sb=5&part=&vc=">Comments</a>?<br></FONT> <font size="-1"><center><a href="#top">-Top-</a></font></center></td></tr></table><br>
